    "observation": "Observe halt_csr_o during WFI, its hold without an interrupt, release on a timer interrupt, and reset. Read MCYCLE/MCYCLEH and MINSTRET/MINSTRETH through csr_rdata_o. Start each low half at 0xfffffffe and check propagation into its high half when it wraps. MINSTRET holds without commit acknowledgement and advances on each acknowledged retirement.",
    "window": "Drive each WFI and timer-release condition for four full clocks before the final observation; hold the no-interrupt state for four clocks after WFI. Inputs change only while the clock is low. This finite window accommodates direct/registered responses and interrupt synchronization; it is not an exact one-cycle or universal maximum latency requirement.",
    "tools": "Python 3, Verilator with --binary/--timing support, C++ compiler and make. No CPU-wide build.",
    "completion": "Exit 0 requires successful build, simulator exit 0 and both fixture PASS markers. The original four CPU/Spike programs must also pass. The fixed bench builds and runs with the reference module, so a build failure, an abnormal end, a missing or incomplete observation record and an explicit mismatch are FAIL (1). Missing fixed tools or inputs, resource exhaustion and wall-clock timeouts are INVALID (2)."
